## SQL Statements

Simplified SQL used by the provider to read this data source.

```sql
-- List the explicit permissions on visible outbound datashares with their producer databases.
SELECT ... FROM svv_datashare_privileges JOIN svv_datashares ... WHERE share_type = 'OUTBOUND' ...;
```

## Read Behavior

`datashare_privileges` is empty when nothing matches; it is ordered by share, grantee type, and grantee. One query in
the provider database covers the shares of every producer database, each reported with its `database_name`. `PUBLIC` is
reported with `grantee = "public"`; the `grantee` filter `public` selects it, and `grantee_type` tells a user and a role
of the same name apart. Permissions held with grant option are reported like any other.

`id` (String, computed) is the listing's provider-relative JSON identity containing the configured filters.

Superusers and users with the `ACCESS SYSTEM TABLE` permission see every grant; other users see only the identities they
have access to or own. Only read-only SQL is executed.
